course: dictionary
lesson: 8592
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Scooter» can mean a toy you push along with one foot, or a small motorbike. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «You walk a scooter down a steep hill, because you can lose control.» Here a scooter is the thing you ride or push. The clues are walk, steep hill and lose control. Nobody walks a motorbike down a hill, so this is the toy or vehicle with a board and a handle.
explain: «A helmet greatly lowers the chance of a serious head injury when cycling, skating or scootering.» Scootering is an activity here, the act of riding a scooter. Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have picked the right one.
fact: A scooter is a toy or vehicle with a narrow board, two small wheels and a long handle, which you push along with one foot.
fact: A motor scooter is a small motorbike with a low seat.
fact: An electric scooter, or e-scooter, has a small motor and a battery.
fact: A scooter has 2 wheels.
fact: Context clues, such as walk, ride, battery or helmet, show you which meaning of a word is meant.
exercise: «When a big boy knocks a little girl off her scooter, Sam runs to the shop on the corner.» What is a scooter in this sentence? | A battery for a phone | A kind of shop | A small motorbike with a low seat | *A toy or vehicle with a narrow board, two small wheels and a long handle
exercise: Mum says «The motor scooter is parked outside.» What is a motor scooter? | A helmet for riding | A toy with a narrow board | *A small motorbike with a low seat | A kind of wheel
exercise: How many wheels does a scooter have? | *Two | Three | One | Four
test: Sam's sister wants an e-scooter with a battery. What is an e-scooter? | A skateboard with a rope | A helmet worn for safety | A bike with a basket | *A scooter with a small motor and a battery
test: Dad says «We need a helmet for the scooter ride to the park.» Why is the helmet needed? | *It lowers the chance of a serious head injury | It is a kind of battery | It makes the scooter go faster | It keeps the scooter dry
exam: The text says «You walk a scooter down a steep hill, because you can lose control.» Why do you walk it rather than ride it? | Because the helmet is too big | *Because you can lose control on a steep hill | Because the battery is flat | Because scooters cannot have wheels on hills
